---
import Num from "../Num.astro";
import Tile from "./Tile.astro";
---

<p class="not-prose mb-5 font-sans text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
  Frozen evaluation · Fall and protective equipment · ConstructionSite10k
</p>
<div class="metrics-grid grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
  <Tile title="Micro-F1 on the final images">
    <Fragment slot="big"
      ><Num k="final.grove.micro_f1" />
      <span class="text-lg">against</span>
      <Num k="final.gemma.micro_f1" /></Fragment
    >
    GROVE against the single-pass model <span class="font-mono">gemma4:31b</span
    >; difference
    <Num k="final.diff.grove_minus_gemma" as="signed" ci /> (95% interval).
  </Tile>
  <Tile title="False alarms per 100 violation-free images">
    <Fragment slot="big"
      ><Num k="final.grove.false_alarms" d={1} />
      <span class="text-lg">against</span>
      <Num k="final.gemma.false_alarms" d={1} /></Fragment
    >
    GROVE against <span class="font-mono">gemma4:31b</span> on the final images.
  </Tile>
  <Tile title="Unseen images, scored once">
    <Fragment slot="big"><Num k="final.n_images" as="int" /></Fragment>
    Final images scored once, after the protocol, models and thresholds were frozen.
  </Tile>
  <Tile title="Top evidence box F1 at IoU 0.5">
    <Fragment slot="big"><Num k="final.box.grove.0.5.f1" /></Fragment>
    GROVE&rsquo;s top box per alert on the final images (<span class="font-mono"
      >gemma4:31b</span
    > boxes as written:
    <Num k="final.box.gemma.0.5.f1" />).
  </Tile>
</div>
